;; What the Unreleased release renames, merges, re-means and retires, as data
;; (docs/catalog.md, "A release's renames").  The release cut renames this file to
;; `<version>.edn`, and `lein lint`'s E22 holds it to the changelog's Breaking
;; entries, the shipped KB and the API goldens.
;;
;; The four top-level keys are KB vocabulary, which `upgrade --sync`
;; (`vaelii.host.sync/rename!`) rewrites in stored premises (`:renames`,
;; `:context-merges`) or reports (`:re-meanings`, `:retired`).  `:api` holds the
;; same kinds for the public API, koinii's vars and the daemon's ops, which a
;; caller's code rewrites.
{:renames        {bijection  bijective_predicate
                  injection  injective_predicate
                  surjection surjective_predicate}
 :context-merges {}
 :re-meanings    {parentOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  childOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  motherOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  fatherOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  siblingOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  grandparentOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."
                  ancestorOf "Unqualified genetic-or-chosen reading; use GeneticKinFn for genetic descent."}
 :retired        #{chosenSiblingOf FatherFn MotherFn}
 :api            {}}
